            {
              "id": "CVE-2023-36054",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "krb5: Denial of service through freeing uninitialized pointer"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "lib/kadm5/kadm_rpc_xdr.c in MIT Kerberos 5 (aka krb5) before 1.20.2 and 1.21.x before 1.21.1 frees an uninitialized pointer. A remote authenticated user can trigger a kadmind crash. This occurs because _xdr_kadm5_principal_ent_rec does not validate the relationship between n_key_data and the key_data array count."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2023-36054",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2023-36054\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: krb5-libs\nFixed Version: 1.20.2-r0\nLink: [CVE-2023-36054](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2023-36054)\nlib/kadm5/kadm_rpc_xdr.c in MIT Kerberos 5 (aka krb5) before 1.20.2 and 1.21.x before 1.21.1 frees an uninitialized pointer. A remote authenticated user can trigger a kadmind crash. This occurs because _xdr_kadm5_principal_ent_rec does not validate the relationship between n_key_data and the key_data array count.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2023-36054**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|krb5-libs|1.20.2-r0|[CVE-2023-36054](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2023-36054)|\n\nlib/kadm5/kadm_rpc_xdr.c in MIT Kerberos 5 (aka krb5) before 1.20.2 and 1.21.x before 1.21.1 frees an uninitialized pointer. A remote authenticated user can trigger a kadmind crash. This occurs because _xdr_kadm5_principal_ent_rec does not validate the relationship between n_key_data and the key_data array count."
              },
